# Let the logged-in session read the power button.
#
# Numbered 72 so it runs after 71-seat.rules and before 73-seat-late.rules.
# 73 runs the uaccess builtin for a tag that is already set, and logind
# retriggers devices with that current tag when the session becomes active.
# Matching only ACTION=="add" runs before anyone is logged in, so the ACL is
# never granted.
#
# The ACPI node named "Power Button" carries only that key. Hide it from
# labwc. Once its tag is current, 71-seat.rules also puts that node on the
# seat, and LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE keeps labwc from treating it as a keyboard.
#
# Some machines report the press on "Intel HID 5 button array" instead. That
# same node carries the volume keys. It stays visible to the session so the
# service can read it. The node is a power switch, not a keyboard, so the
# service changes the volume from those keys. Keyboard volume keys are bound
# in labwc.
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Power Button", TAG+="uaccess", ENV{LIBINPUT_IGNORE_DEVICE}="1"
SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", ATTRS{name}=="Intel HID 5 button array", TAG+="uaccess"
